17:["$","div","2",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Label in the room, immediately after collection, in the patient's presence, checking the armband. Never pre-label containers and never carry unlabelled specimens out to label later. Both are how specimens are switched, and the consequence lands on two patients at once."]}]
18:["$","p","3",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"A clean-catch midstream urine specimen minimizes contamination from skin and perineal flora. The patient cleans the area front to back with the provided wipes, begins urinating into the toilet, then passes the container into the stream mid-flow without touching the inside of the container or lid, and finishes in the toilet. Instructions given clearly are what determine whether the specimen is usable."}]
